was set aside because 'foot' plainly writes regel.", "source": ["WLC.PSA.110.1.017", "WLC.PSA.110.1.018", "WLC.PSA.110.1.019"], "source_head": "WLC.PSA.110.1.017", "status": "aligned", "target": ["t022"], "target_head": "t022"}, {"id": "PSA.110.1.a018", "note": "Suffix on 'feet' realized as the 'thy' of 'thy footstool' (rule 18).", "source": ["WLC.PSA.110.1.020"], "source_head": "WLC.PSA.110.1.020", "status": "aligned", "target": ["t021"], "target_head": "t021"}], "ref": "PSA.110.1", "review_notes": ["Superscription 'A Psalm of David' aligned token by token; ne'um YHWH recast as 'Jehovah saith'.", "Corrected: hadom + le + ragle fused into one unit on 'footstool' (rules 30, 23, 22), rather than leaving the lamed and regel unrepresented; the suffix keeps 'thy'."], "source_edition": "ASV-alignment Hebrew projection", "target_edition": "ASV", "variant_decisions": []}
